# Authorized edge keys: one per line, an OpenSSH authorized_keys line prefixed
# with the clientId the key authenticates as. Lines starting with '#' and blank
# lines are ignored. Keys are matched by SHA-256 fingerprint.
#
# Format:
#   <clientId> <openssh-public-key>
#
# Generate an edge keypair:
#   ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f edge-clientA -C clientA
# then paste the contents of edge-clientA.pub after the clientId:
#
# clientA ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIExampleExampleExampleExampleExampleExa clientA
# clientB ssh-rsa AAAAB3NzaC1yc2EAAAADAQABAAABgQDExample... clientB
#
# Copy this file to config/authorized_edges (gitignored) and add your real keys.
